hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1635","Narrated Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (RA): He reported, \"In the narration transmitted by Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah (RA): Mu'adh ibn Jabal (RA) used to pray the 'Isha (night) prayer with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), then he would return and pray with his companions. Abu Bakr (RA) then said: 'I have fully detailed this matter in its entirety, and I have clarified therein the reports of the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding the prayer of fear (Salat al-Khawf): that the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed with one of the two groups as a voluntary (nafl) prayer, while they prayed behind him an obligatory (fard) prayer for themselves. Thus, it was a voluntary prayer for the Prophet (ﷺ) and an obligatory one for them.'\""
